>> title: Soy Sauce Chicken, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, chinese, soy sauce, poached, whole bird, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: soy-sauce-chicken
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: see yao gai, si yau gai, 豉油雞, soya chicken, soy sauce chicken, lou sui gai, slow cooker soy sauce chicken, crockpot poached chicken
>> servings: 4
>> time: 4 hr 40 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the breast goes dry and stringy in the same pot that made the thighs perfect, and there is no reversing it

Nothing is browned and nothing may be: the colour comes from dark soy. The stock goes into the crock hot.

>> step: simmer the lou sui 20 min on the stove
Simmer @water{5%cups}(1.2 L) with @light soy sauce{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL), @dark soy sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @Shaoxing wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @rock sugar{4%oz}(115 g), @star anise{3%pods}, @cassia bark{1%stick}, @dried tangerine peel{1%piece}, @fresh ginger{6%slices}(coin-sized), @scallions{3}(knotted) in a #saucepan{} for ~simmer{20%min}, until the sugar has gone and the spices have opened.

>> step: poach on low, 4 hr
Slow cook @whole chicken{3 1/2%lb}(1.6 kg; rinsed and dried) breast-down in @&(~1)master stock{}, poured over it hot in a #slow cooker{}, on low for ~slow cook{4%hr}, the bird submerged to the shoulders and the lid on.

>> step: rest 20 min, brush with sesame oil, chop
Rest @&(~1)chicken{} in the pot off ~rest{20%min}, lift it out, brush with @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp} and chop through the bone. Keep the strained lou sui: chilled, fat off, boiled up weekly.
